From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wtsapi32: session notifications and lock state from the session's compositor

WTSRegisterSessionNotification(Ex) and WTSUnRegisterSessionNotification(Ex)
were stubs and no WM_WTSSESSION_CHANGE was ever sent. Chrome, Edge,
Firefox and VS Code register for it: they stop timers and media, blank
sensitive content and reconnect when the session is locked or unlocked.

- The session's compositor (sg-compositor 0.2.0+sg51) follows the session
  on its control socket for the session's programs (SESSION): the state at
  once, then lock, unlock, Remote Desktop taking the session and giving it
  back, and a remote viewer starting and stopping. The socket is the
  session's SG_LOCK_CONTROL, else the one the session puts up for this
  user. A new unix library (wtsapi32.so) connects and reads it.
- A process with registrations follows it on a thread of its own (started
  by the first registration, which returns once it follows, so a lock
  right after registering is not lost; it reconnects every 5 s while
  anything is registered if the compositor is not there or went away) and
  sends WM_WTSSESSION_CHANGE (lParam the session) to the registered
  windows: WTS_SESSION_LOCK and WTS_SESSION_UNLOCK; WTS_CONSOLE_DISCONNECT
  and WTS_REMOTE_CONNECT when Remote Desktop takes the session,
  WTS_REMOTE_DISCONNECT and WTS_CONSOLE_CONNECT when it gives it back (it
  comes back locked: WTS_SESSION_LOCK); WTS_SESSION_REMOTE_CONTROL when a
  remote viewer starts or stops. There is one session: a registration for
  all sessions gets the same, and no other session logs on or off.
- Bad flags or no such window: ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER; the Ex forms take
  only WTS_CURRENT_SERVER_HANDLE. Unregistering a window not registered is
  ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER.
- WTSQuerySessionInformation: WTSSessionInfoEx (not implemented) with the
  lock state in SessionFlags (WTS_SESSIONSTATE_LOCK / UNLOCK);
  WTSClientProtocolType (a FIXME giving 0) is RDP's while Remote Desktop
  has the session; WTSIsRemoteSession; WTSSessionInfo's FIXME goes.
- winuser.h: the WTS_* session change codes; wtsapi32.h: WTSINFOEX,
  WTS_SESSIONSTATE_* and NOTIFY_FOR_*.

Gate: test/wtsnotify-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/wtsnotify-probe.c with a
stand-in control socket, test/wtsnotify-standin.py; sg-compositor's
test-wtsevents covers the real one; checked end to end against it).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_SESSION_EVENTS, SG_MUTANT_NO_LOCK_STATE
(wtsapi32/wtsapi32.c). Wine's wtsapi32 test: no failures.
---
--- a/dlls/wtsapi32/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/wtsapi32/Makefile.in
@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@
 MODULE    = wtsapi32.dll
+UNIXLIB   = wtsapi32.so
 IMPORTLIB = wtsapi32
-IMPORTS   = advapi32
+IMPORTS   = advapi32 user32
 
 SOURCES = \
+	unixlib.c \
 	wtsapi32.c
